ses value\n\nReason:\nI have a Queen-high straight, which is a very strong hand. My opponent has checked through every street and only called my turn bet, showing significant weakness. While there's a risk they have a King for the nut straight, their passive play makes this unlikely. A moderate value bet of 200-400 chips can extract value from weaker hands (pairs, Ace-high, or even a Queen that splits the pot but might call thinking I'm bluffing). Checking wastes the value of my strong hand. I'll bet 300 to get value while not overcommitting if they surprisingly have the King.\n\nAnswer: 300"}
